  "rule": "KPF-18 item 2 (KPF-18.0e): bit-identity of fork-from-checkpoint vs the source's own continuation is NOT owed when KV cell placement differs (GPU batch non-invariance; CPU/Gemma: 0.04 nats at token 1). Judge every fork-vs-own pair against the measured A/A floor: the source's own continuation from the same checkpoint run twice from an identical reseeded state (same slot history, same batch composition). A pair is OK iff first-token top-1 agrees AND first-token top-k max-abs prob and coarse KL are no larger than the A/A maximum (lifted to FLOOR_EPS) AND the identical-greedy-prefix length is no shorter than the shortest A/A prefix. If EVERY A/A pair is bit-identical (floor zero) bit-identity is owed and every fork pair must also be bit-identical. No A/A control => UNJUDGEABLE (rule result None), never a pass. Counts are reported, not a pass word; the A/A control rate is the floor every item-2 number is read against.",
